{% comment %}
  What "Ka" means - the brand's thesis, from Santosh's brand overview doc.

  This exists because the site already carries the idea everywhere and never
  explains it: the rail of letterforms running down the side of every page, and
  the ring of symbols around the cup in the logo, are the same thing - the
  letter "ka" written in thirteen Indian scripts. Without a word of explanation
  a visitor reads them as decoration. With it, they're the reason the company
  has this name.

  The glyphs are the same thirteen the rail uses, rendered from
  snippets/ka-rail-icon.liquid so there is one source of truth: change a
  letterform there and it changes in both places.

  On scale: each glyph carries an inline width/height that sizes it to a shared
  566px^2 area rather than a shared box, because fitting a wide glyph and a tall
  one into the same square shrinks them by very different amounts and Santosh
  flagged that some scripts were reading smaller than others. Scaling every
  glyph by one factor keeps that balance exactly, so this uses `zoom` - which,
  unlike `transform: scale()`, actually takes part in layout, so the grid still
  flows. The @supports fallback is for browsers without it: the glyphs stay
  small but readable rather than vanishing.
{% endcomment %}

{%- comment -%}
  The letterform backdrop rides on the theme's own section-background element,
  which is already exactly viewport-wide and absolutely positioned, so the
  artwork gets its full bleed for free.

  It ships as an alpha mask rather than a picture - see
  scripts/build-ka-pattern.py - so the glyphs take whatever colour is set
  under them rather than one baked into a PNG. One file serves a blush field
  on white here and a cream one on a dark band, with no second asset.

  The colour is its own setting rather than the scheme's foreground: a
  backdrop is a flat colour of its own, and reaching it by fading the text
  colour down gives a grey of that hue, never the blush this wants.

  The URL has to be handed to the CSS from here: {% stylesheet %} is static
  and never sees Liquid, so asset_url can't be written inside it.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div
  class="section-background color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} why-ka__bg{% if section.settings.show_pattern %} why-ka__bg--pattern{% endif %}"
  {%- if section.settings.show_pattern %}
    style="--ka-pattern: url('{{ 'ka-pattern.png' | asset_url }}'); --ka-pattern-opacity: {{ section.settings.pattern_opacity | divided_by: 100.0 }};{% if section.settings.pattern_color != blank %} --ka-pattern-ink: {{ section.settings.pattern_color }};{% endif %}"
  {%- endif %}
></div>
<div
  class="section section--{{ section.settings.section_width }} color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} why-ka spacing-style"
  style="{%- render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}"
>
  <div class="why-ka__inner">
    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <h2 class="why-ka__heading">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}
      <div class="why-ka__body rte">{{ section.settings.body }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    The glyph grid sits outside __inner so it can use the section's full width.
    Inside the text column it left a void to the right of every paragraph.

    Behind a setting because the homepage currently runs without it - Santosh
    is working on something to put in its place - while Our Story still shows
    the full specimen sheet. The caption is inside the same condition: on its
    own it describes letters that aren't there.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if section.settings.show_glyphs -%}
    <div class="why-ka__glyphs" role="img" aria-label="{{ section.settings.glyph_alt | escape }}">
      {%- for i in (0..12) -%}
        <span class="why-ka__glyph">{%- render 'ka-rail-icon', index: i -%}</span>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    {%- if section.settings.caption != blank -%}
      <p class="why-ka__caption">{{ section.settings.caption }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if section.settings.closing != blank -%}
    <p class="why-ka__closing">{{ section.settings.closing }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .why-ka__bg {
    position: relative;
  }

  /* A wave divider is its own section, and the part of it below the curve is
     flat background - so a field that starts at this section's own top edge
     leaves a bare strip between the trough of the wave and the first glyph,
     which reads as a gap rather than as a margin. The field rises by the
     wave's height and is covered by its solid fill, so it starts at the curve
     itself. The rise is the wave's own svg height; see snippets/wave-divider. */
  #MainContent > div.shopify-section:has(.wave-divider) + div.shopify-section .why-ka__bg--pattern {
    --ka-pattern-rise: 72px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    #MainContent > div.shopify-section:has(.wave-divider) + div.shopify-section .why-ka__bg--pattern {
      --ka-pattern-rise: 124px;
    }
  }

  /* The mask is what makes this a texture rather than a picture: the PNG
     carries only an alpha channel, and the colour under it is the scheme's
     own foreground, so the glyphs come out cream on the dark band and brown
     on a light one without a second file.

     `cover` rather than a tile. The artwork is one composition, not a
     repeating unit - its edges cut through letterforms, so repeating it would
     draw a seam straight down the section. One copy, cropped. */
  .why-ka__bg--pattern::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    top: calc(-1 * var(--ka-pattern-rise, 0px));
    background-color: var(--ka-pattern-ink, var(--color-foreground, currentColor));
    -webkit-mask-image: var(--ka-pattern);
    mask-image: var(--ka-pattern);
    -webkit-mask-size: cover;
    mask-size: cover;
    -webkit-mask-position: center;
    mask-position: center;
    -webkit-mask-repeat: no-repeat;
    mask-repeat: no-repeat;
    opacity: var(--ka-pattern-opacity, 0.12);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  /* Sized to the prose itself, so the text column has no orphan space beside
     it. The glyph grid is a sibling and uses the section's full width. */
  .why-ka__inner {
    max-width: 38rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .why-ka__heading {
    font-family: var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: clamp(1.875rem, 3.6vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .why-ka__body p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .why-ka__body p:last-child {
    margin-block-end: 0;
  }

  /* The thirteen letterforms, as a specimen sheet. Centred because the point
     is the set, not any one of them. */
  .why-ka__glyphs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    margin-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem) 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-primary, currentColor);
  }

  .why-ka__glyph {
    display: inline-flex;
    /* Preserves the per-glyph equal-area sizing set in ka-rail-icon.liquid;
       see the comment at the top of this file. */
    zoom: 3.4;
  }

  @supports not (zoom: 2) {
    .why-ka__glyph svg {
      height: 4.25rem;
      width: auto;
    }
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .why-ka__glyph {
      zoom: 2.4;
    }

    @supports not (zoom: 2) {
      .why-ka__glyph svg {
        height: 3rem;
      }
    }
  }

  .why-ka__caption {
    margin: 0;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  .why-ka__closing {
    font-family: var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.2vw, 1.75rem);
    line-height: 1.3;
    text-align: center;
    text-wrap: balance;
    margin: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem) auto 0;
    max-width: 30rem;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Why Ka",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Every Indian language begins with the same letter" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "body", "label": "Body" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_glyphs", "label": "Show the letterform specimen sheet", "info": "The thirteen scripts and their caption, under the text.", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "glyph_alt", "label": "Glyph grid description", "default": "The letter ka, written in thirteen Indian scripts" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "caption", "label": "Caption under the letters" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "closing", "label": "Closing line" },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_pattern",
      "label": "Letterform backdrop",
      "info": "The field of ka glyphs behind the section, painted in the scheme's own text colour.",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "pattern_color",
      "label": "Backdrop colour",
      "info": "The colour the letterforms are drawn in. Left empty, they take the scheme's text colour.",
      "default": "#f7ebe7"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "pattern_opacity",
      "label": "Backdrop strength",
      "min": 10,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100
    },
    { "type": "color_scheme", "id": "color_scheme", "label": "Color scheme", "default": "scheme-2" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "section_width",
      "label": "Width",
      "options": [
        { "value": "page-width", "label": "Page" },
        { "value": "full-width", "label": "Full" }
      ],
      "default": "page-width"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Padding" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-start", "label": "Top", "min": 0, "max": 160, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 80 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-end", "label": "Bottom", "min": 0, "max": 160, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 80 }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Why Ka" }]
}
{% endschema %}
